
🚀 Day 7 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved two LeetCode problems and strengthened my understanding of the Two Pointers technique by applying it to both string processing and in-place array manipulation.

🟢 LeetCode 125 – Valid Palindrome

💡 Approach: Two Pointers + Character Filtering

I used two pointers starting from both ends of the string. Before comparing characters, I skipped all non-alphanumeric characters and converted uppercase letters to lowercase using tolower(). This ensured that only valid characters were compared while maintaining an efficient solution.

📚 What I Learned:
✅ Applying the Two Pointers technique on strings
✅ Filtering non-alphanumeric characters efficiently
✅ Using tolower() for case-insensitive comparison
✅ Improving string-processing logic with optimized traversal
✅ Achieving O(n) time complexity with O(1) extra space

🟢 LeetCode 344 – Reverse String

💡 Approach: Two Pointers (In-Place Swapping)

I placed one pointer at the beginning and another at the end of the character array. By swapping the characters and moving both pointers toward the center, I reversed the string in-place without using any additional memory.

📚 What I Learned:
✅ Mastering the Two Pointers technique for arrays
✅ Reversing data efficiently using swap()
✅ Performing in-place operations with O(1) extra space
✅ Understanding pointer movement for optimal solutions

